<title>SOUTH AFRICA: M&amp;R half year shr falls but div held.</title>
<headline>M&amp;R half year shr falls but div held.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   18.0	  vs	52.0</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     42.0	  vs	52.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 14.5	  vs	14.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   145	   vs	177</p>
<p>Profit on sale of</p>
<p>     businesses	     79	    vs	3 loss</p>
<p>Profit on sale of</p>
<p>     property		 3	     vs	4</p>
<p>Attrib less non-operating</p>
<p>     profits on disposals 63	    vs	178</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   195	   vs	264</p>
<p>    Tax			 31	    vs	71</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   151	   vs	82</p>
<p>    Turnover		  6,076	 vs	5,171</p>
<p>Div payable April 25</p>
<p>On register April 4</p>
<p>Full name: Murray and Roberts Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast EPS of 26.6 cents with the range 23.2-31.0 and a dividend of 14.5.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
